PROBATUS TECHNOLOGIES ANNOUNCES UDEVIX ALLIANCE FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE
GLOBAL LINUX COMMUNITY
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-----------------

Turku, Finland - September 17, 2002. Leading Linux vendor Probatus
Technologies announced today its global uDevix Alliance. This unprecedented
partnership program invites Linux software providers into a joint industry
effort for the benefit of the Linux community.

Progression in the field of computing and information technology does not
take place unless there are companies with visions of how things could and
should be. The new uDevix Alliance is the realization of a strong vision
concerning a united Linux software industry.

"As a company developing a professional Linux operating environment, we
realized there was a need for someone to bring together the excellent
software products that truly enable the developers to use Linux for serious
business," said Raimo Koski, a well-acknowledged Linux developer, author and
researcher at Probatus Technologies. "Instead of letting the developers to
laboriously search for suitable software, we are now able to present them
with an outstanding set of standards compliant solutions in a certified,
production-ready package. And consequently, developers will be better
equipped to create usable products for the markets. All in all, the uDevix
Alliance gives a unique chance for the Linux community to raise awareness
concerning the suitability of Linux for productive work and to provide the
markets with better Linux solutions."

Currently, there are over twenty companies in the uDevix Alliance. Solid
Information Technology (see http://www.solidtech.com/aboutus/pr_78.html),
Runtime Revolution (see http://www.runrev.com/company/pressreleases/9.html),
SoftIntegration, Inc., No Magic, Inc., and Lifix Systems have already
announced their support for this joint industry effort. In addition, a
pioneering selection of state-of-the-art Linux software from the vendors who
have joined the alliance is included in Probatus Spectra(TM) Linux 1.2, the
newest version of Probatus� operating environment designed for robust data
processing.

The Probatus Spectra(TM) uDevix and Probatus Spectra(TM) uOffix disks
provided in the Spectra Linux 1.2 distribution offer valuable resources to
the developers around the world. Database management and data migration
utilities, multi-platform development applications, code debugging and
optimization software, PDF creation and management tools, and several office
suites are among the included products.

The Certification Group at Probatus tests each included software product to
be compatible with the Spectra Linux environment. "The Certified for
Probatus Spectra(TM) Linux approval gives these products an added mark of
reliability as the end-users can be certain that the development tool and
the underlying platform are compatible with each other," Mr. Koski
continued.

"By uniting the world�s leading software vendors in such an exceptional way,
we can really ensure the next phase of professional computing. In effect,
what we are able to provide the global Linux community with is a most
powerful set of certified development and productivity tools of the next
generation," said Esa Tervo, Chief Technology Officer of Probatus
Technologies. "The strong foundation that the uDevix Alliance already forms
should awaken the interest of the whole enterprise: the executive level, the
developers, and the software retailers. We are happy to welcome all
organizations interested in joining this effort from which the whole Linux
community can benefit."

More information about the uDevix Alliance can be requested by contacting
partners@probatus.com. Information about the availability of Probatus
Spectra(TM) Linux 1.2 can be obtained from sales@probatus.com.


