Hello,

Konserve is a small backup application for the KDE 3.x environment.
It lives in the system tray and is able to create backups of several
directories or files periodically.

You can get it on:

    http://www.eikon.tum.de/~hermes/konserve.html.

There is also a link to the documentation and screenshots.

Features new in version 0.7:
* KDE standard network transparency is used for saving the backup
  copies on the local filesystem or on a remote computer
* A wizard is available, which helps the user to create a backup
  profile step by step.
* Lost files or directories can be restored from previously made
  backups with just one mouse click.
* The Preferences dialog makes sure that unsaved changes are
  preserved.
* Periodic creation of backup can be started in the Preferences menu
* hidden archives are not hidden any more. The are prepended with
  a literal 'dot'

Special thanks this time go to Michael Bieligk for creating those
lovely graphics used in the wizard and on the Konserve web site.

Enjoy!

