Benaulim,
24th September 2002
1.05 am

Hey everybody,

Wanting to reach out to a greater audience and fed up of waiting for the
main Linux Group to come online, a few of us decided to talk less and
work more. We wanted to surprise everybody so that explains the
suddenness. ;-)

It's finally out! After just three frantic days of secret discussions,
secret meets, online chats and of course secret exchange of info, Rodney
Almeida, Andrew Suares and myself have jointly launched a website for
ILUG Margao.

The past three days have been hectic with ideas, discussions and debates
keeping us working through the day and night, burning the midnight oil
upto 2 am! At first, we did not know what to put on...and where...and
even choosing a name for the site.

We had a deadline...Saturday night, and Andrew did hoist the site right
on time, but due to the site being on a free server, we had a barrage of
pop up windows to battle through before we actually saw tux the penguin.
We all agreed, that the site needed much more info before it went
public....but what? :-) Then another problem...the web server was having
trouble with uploading the files from our computers!

But many hands make light work. I got down to searching my hard disk for
relevant info and began compiling some stuff. A call to Fred helped and
in came some more info. While this was going on, Andrew designed the web
pages, checked if they displayed properly in IE, Netscape, and Opera.
Rodney graciously offered to use some of his web space and host the
website. He did the groundwork, and uploading of files. Phone calls
flying across every hour from Benaulim to Margao to Seraulim... :-)

Finally, we had something presentable. And even while I finish writing
this announcement, there's one guy making the finishing touches and
another uploading files.

We know we may have or will have made a few mistakes here and there, so
please be kind enough to point out our mistakes *politely* :-), and even
better, to offer to help rectify those mistakes ;-). Advice, help and
info for the site is *most* welcome. You can contact us at:
Rodney Almeida Jr.	(rodney@rodneysroses.com)
Andrew Suares		(andrew_suares@gmx.net)
Clinton Vaz			(klintvaz@gmx.net)

And finally, Welcome to ILUG-Margao's own Website, it at
http://ilug-margao.cjb.net/

Clinton..

